{title: In Our Own Eyes We Seemed Like Grasshoppers}
{subtitle: Numbers 13:7; 13:21–25; 13:28–33; 14:1–4; 14:36–38}
{key: D#m}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] |
| [D#m] | [C#] | [D#m] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[B]Twelve [C#]men went [D#m]out from [B]the camp
From the [C#]tribe of Is[D#m]sachar Igal [B]came
To scout the [C#]land from Zin [D#m]to Rehob
They cut [C#]a branch [D#m]in the [B]Valley of Es[C#]hcol
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Forty days [D#m]they walked the [B]ground
And saw the [C#]cities for[D#m]tified [B]and strong
The [C#]descendants of [D#m]Anak [B]lived there
We [C#]seemed like gras[D#m]shoppers [B]in their sight
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The people [C#]who live there are [D#m]strong
The c[B]ities are [C#]forti[D#m]fied and very [B]large
We [C#]cannot at[D#m]tack those people
They are stron[C#]ger than we [D#m]are
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
The [B]whole congre[C#]gation broke out in [D#m]cry
[B]And wept through [C#]that long and heavy [D#m]night
Why [B]bring us [C#]to this land to [D#m]die
Let [B]us choose a [C#]leader and [D#m]go back
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[B]The people who live there [C#]are strong
The [D#m]cities are [B]fortified [C#]and ve[D#m]ry large
We can[B]not at[C#]tack those peo[D#m]ple
[B]They are stronger [C#]than we [D#m]are
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Spread[B]ing a bad re[C#]port on the [D#m]land
They [B]made the congrega[C#]tion grumble and [D#m]cry
Before [B]the Lord a plague [C#]fell down
Only [D#m]Joshua and Caleb [B]remained
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Only [C#]Joshua and Ca[D#m]leb remained
{end_of_verse}
